        ddc::is_discrete_element_v&lt;T&gt;&amp;&amp; std::is_same_v&lt;ddc::coordinate_of_t&lt;T&gt;, CoordType&gt;)    </initializer>
    <briefdescription>
<para>A concept satisfied by a coordinate of type CoordType, or by an index whose coordinate is of type CoordType. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This is useful for operators which can be evaluated either at an arbitrary coordinate or at a grid point. Evaluating at a grid point allows the operator to use precomputed values where they are available.</para>
